  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative launched on June 15th with a $500,000 Phase 1 budget led by Sarah Tan. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate and recently reached its first major milestone with a successfully tested secure file sharing prototype. The team has expanded with new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing. Upcoming activities include a meeting on August 5th to discuss AI-driven efficiency gains, the start of the development phase next month led by Omar Jensen, user interface enhancements in October, and the commencement of training sessions next month. Security protocols are being updated for January, and the team is preparing for an onboarding session on September 10th."
